{
  "b45a92d7463a65d12ac7b88c0b4f105e_0": {
    "author": "Zuful",
    "comment": "execRunner.Run: name is the literal \"docker\" at every call site and exec.CommandContext never invokes a shell, so argv entries cannot be reinterpreted as commands. The residual argument-injection risk (a name read as a flag) is closed by validateComposeName, which rejects any project or service name not matching ^[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9_.-]*$ before it reaches this call. See the matching #nosec G204 in dockercompose.go.",
    "false_positive": true,
    "ignored_at": "2026-09-25T18:09:11Z"
  },
  "6185ed238ac9431ee9fa50d1c44c493d_0": {
    "author": "Zuful",
    "comment": "health.LoadSettings: the path comes from RIKUGAN_HEALTH_CONFIG, set by the operator who runs rikugan, with the same trust as KUBECONFIG or PROMETHEUS_URL. No MCP request or remote input reaches it, and the file is only parsed as YAML into a typed struct with unknown keys rejected. See the matching #nosec G304 in settings.go.",
    "false_positive": true,
    "ignored_at": "2026-10-18T14:05:00Z"
  },
  "bfa5df24b0eb1b8fd7b996c3e98aab8f_0": {
    "author": "Zuful",
    "comment": "journal.replayFile: the path is the operator's state directory (RIKUGAN_STATE_DIR, same trust as KUBECONFIG) joined with either the fixed name verdicts.jsonl or a rotated name the journal lists itself and accepts only if it parses as verdicts-<timestamp>.jsonl. No MCP request or remote input reaches it. See the matching #nosec G304 in journal.go.",
    "false_positive": true,
    "ignored_at": "2026-10-18T20:40:00Z"
  }
}
